--- TIM-22, TIM-23, TIM-24..TIM-27, TIM-31, TIM-33..TIM-38: timer lifecycle, bare creation, milliseconds wait ---
Get current time into pantry.
a timer called 'the sketchpad'.
If 'the sketchpad's running then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 0 got {'the sketchpad's running}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's running.
Start 'the sketchpad'.
If 'the sketchpad's running is false then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 1 got {'the sketchpad's running}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's running.
Wait 49 milliseconds.
finish 'the sketchpad'.
If 'the sketchpad's running then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 0 got {'the sketchpad's running}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's running.
Get current time into 'the inbox'.
If 'the sketchpad's duration in milliseconds is less than 49 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-15: expected at least 49 got {'the sketchpad's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-15 ok".
If 'the sketchpad's duration in milliseconds is greater than 5049 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-15: expected at most 5049 got {'the sketchpad's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-15 ok".
If 'the sketchpad's duration in milliseconds is less than 'the sketchpad's duration in seconds multiply 1000 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-36: expected at least {'the sketchpad's duration in seconds multiply 1000} got {'the sketchpad's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-36 ok".
If 'the sketchpad's duration in milliseconds is greater than 'the sketchpad's duration in seconds multiply 1000 add 1000 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-37: expected at most {'the sketchpad's duration in seconds multiply 1000 add 1000} got {'the sketchpad's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-37 ok".
If 'the sketchpad's start time is less than pantry's unix then, Print "ASSERT TIM-33: expected at least {pantry's unix} got {'the sketchpad's start time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-33 ok".
If 'the sketchpad's end time is less than 'the sketchpad's start time then, Print "ASSERT TIM-34: expected at least {'the sketchpad's start time} got {'the sketchpad's end time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-34 ok".
If 'the sketchpad's end time is greater than 'the inbox's unix then, Print "ASSERT TIM-38: expected at most {'the inbox's unix} got {'the sketchpad's end time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-38 ok".

--- the same leaf, seed 12: Create form, seconds-flavour wait ---
Get current time into 'outgoing post'.
Create a timer called 'the postbag'.
If 'the postbag's running then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 0 got {'the postbag's running}", Exit 95. Print 'the postbag's running.
start the 'the postbag'.
If 'the postbag's running is false then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 1 got {'the postbag's running}", Exit 95. Print 'the postbag's running.
Sleep for 0 seconds.
Finish the 'the postbag'.
If 'the postbag's running then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 0 got {'the postbag's running}", Exit 95. Print 'the postbag's running.
Get current time into 'the pigeonhole'.
If 'the postbag's duration in milliseconds is less than 0 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-15: expected at least 0 got {'the postbag's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-15 ok".
If 'the postbag's duration in milliseconds is greater than 5000 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-15: expected at most 5000 got {'the postbag's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-15 ok".
If 'the postbag's duration in milliseconds is less than 'the postbag's duration in seconds multiply 1000 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-36: expected at least {'the postbag's duration in seconds multiply 1000} got {'the postbag's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-36 ok".
If 'the postbag's duration in milliseconds is greater than 'the postbag's duration in seconds multiply 1000 add 1000 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-37: expected at most {'the postbag's duration in seconds multiply 1000 add 1000} got {'the postbag's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-37 ok".
If 'the postbag's start time is less than 'outgoing post's unix then, Print "ASSERT TIM-33: expected at least {'outgoing post's unix} got {'the postbag's start time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-33 ok".
If 'the postbag's end time is less than 'the postbag's start time then, Print "ASSERT TIM-34: expected at least {'the postbag's start time} got {'the postbag's end time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-34 ok".
If 'the postbag's end time is greater than 'the pigeonhole's unix then, Print "ASSERT TIM-38: expected at most {'the pigeonhole's unix} got {'the postbag's end time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-38 ok".

--- the same leaf, seed 834: the wait-flavour bug's own repro seed ---
Get current time into 'the register'.
Create a timer called 'cupboard'.
If 'cupboard's running then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 0 got {'cupboard's running}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard's running.
begin 'cupboard'.
If 'cupboard's running is false then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 1 got {'cupboard's running}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard's running.
Wait 94 millisecond.
stop 'cupboard'.
If 'cupboard's running then, Print "ASSERT TIM-35: expected 0 got {'cupboard's running}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard's running.
Get current time into 'ledger'.
If 'cupboard's duration in milliseconds is less than 94 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-15: expected at least 94 got {'cupboard's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-15 ok".
If 'cupboard's duration in milliseconds is greater than 5094 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-15: expected at most 5094 got {'cupboard's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-15 ok".
If 'cupboard's duration in milliseconds is less than 'cupboard's duration in seconds multiply 1000 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-36: expected at least {'cupboard's duration in seconds multiply 1000} got {'cupboard's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-36 ok".
If 'cupboard's duration in milliseconds is greater than 'cupboard's duration in seconds multiply 1000 add 1000 then, Print "ASSERT TIM-37: expected at most {'cupboard's duration in seconds multiply 1000 add 1000} got {'cupboard's duration in milliseconds}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-37 ok".
If 'cupboard's start time is less than 'the register's unix then, Print "ASSERT TIM-33: expected at least {'the register's unix} got {'cupboard's start time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-33 ok".
If 'cupboard's end time is less than 'cupboard's start time then, Print "ASSERT TIM-34: expected at least {'cupboard's start time} got {'cupboard's end time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-34 ok".
If 'cupboard's end time is greater than 'ledger's unix then, Print "ASSERT TIM-38: expected at most {'ledger's unix} got {'cupboard's end time}", Exit 95. Print "TIM-38 ok".

